    <item>
      <title>Chapter 1, Part 3 – Paradigms of Programming Languages</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/courses/compiler/ch1/part3/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 19 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/courses/compiler/ch1/part3/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;imperative--procedural-paradigm&#34;&gt;Imperative / Procedural Paradigm&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Also called the &lt;strong&gt;Von Neumann model&lt;/strong&gt;, based on single processor sequential execution of instructions. Languages in this paradigm are characterized by:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Sequential execution of instructions&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Using variables to represent memory locations&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Using assignment statements to change a variable&amp;rsquo;s value&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Pascal and C are designed around this paradigm.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example: GCD in Pascal&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;function gcd(x,y:integer):integer;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;Begin&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;  If (x = y) then&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    gcd:=x&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;  else&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    if (x &amp;gt; y) then&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;      gcd:=gcd(x-y,y)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    else&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;      gcd:=gcd(x,y-x);&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;End&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Same program in C&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
